WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.076
iGhost turns a website task into a usability
walkthrough. This example uses a fictional local
site and scripted model decisions.

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.653
Mara is an impatient first-time visitor,
checking whether she can try the product before
paying.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.907
Generate walkthrough builds a playable replay
from screenshots and cursor positions.

4
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.917
On the homepage, Get started gives no clear
promise of a free trial.

5
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.045
It leads to two paid plans. The scripted visitor
cannot find a trial.

6
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.321
The suggested fixes: show the starting price
earlier, and make the next step clear.

7
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.997
The generated Codex prompt includes the task,
recommendations, and replay evidence.

8
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.143
We inspect the prompt here. Nothing is sent to
GitHub.

9
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.312
This connects a user task, recorded friction,
and a concrete change request for review.

10
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:13.275
The replay is a real app output. The visitor's
judgments are scripted, so live model quality
remains untested.
